      "writtenOn": "2022-08-19T15:35:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That seems analogous to how we\u0027re handling RenderPassTasks, where the CommandBuffer takes the data and does what it wants. Eventually `renderPietScene` could move up to the top-level CB when we have other backends supported, right?\n\nIt would also mean that the need for a PietRenderer is reduced, if I\u0027m understanding this CL correctly. PietRenderTask wouldn\u0027t need to store a fRenderer anymore, and any internal sharing of the queue/command buffer between our use and piet\u0027s is hidden underneath the CB implementation.\n\nMaybe we can\u0027t quite go that far if Piet isn\u0027t thread safe and the skgpu::piet::MtlRenderer is per recorder.",
      "parentUuid": "07053265_9aa361d7",
      "range": {
